{
  "$comment": [
    "The calibration corpus, pinned by commit so the study is re-runnable.",
    "",
    "Selection criteria, and the reason for each:",
    "  - Spans the languages the floor actually reads. Calibrating on Python",
    "    and applying the result to Java would be the same error D11 and D12",
    "    made about rule coverage.",
    "  - Spans two orders of magnitude of size, because the sqrt(LOC/1000)",
    "    dampener is an invented normalizer and a corpus of similarly-sized",
    "    repositories cannot tell us whether it works.",
    "  - Well-known, actively maintained projects, following the shape MA used",
    "    at 0.5.0 (django, pytest, black, tornado, httpx, lodash, svelte,",
    "    fastapi).",
    "",
    "KNOWN BIAS, stated rather than discovered later: these are all",
    "well-maintained OSS projects with their own security processes. The",
    "distribution measured here is cleaner than the population this tool will",
    "actually be pointed at. A median calibrated to earn a B here means 'as",
    "clean as a well-run OSS project', not 'average code'. That is a defensible",
    "target but it is a choice, and it is D5's to record."
  ],
